{
 "name": "paged-compliance",
 "integration": "drata",
 "description": "The compliance-check mapping, the owner block, and a genuine two-page advance -- the three paths no other scenario exercised, which is exactly where a real tenant's shape could diverge unobserved (real Drata devices virtually always carry compliance checks). Page 1 is exactly the page size (50 rows) so the walk must genuinely advance to page 2 and stop on the short page; requests_absent proves no page 3. Asset 601 carries all six known check types plus a seventh (SCREEN_RECORDING_BLOCKED) Drata could introduce tomorrow: the unknown type must be LOGGED, not abort the run -- the historical defect here concatenated the Starlark builtin `type` into the message and took the whole import down. Asset 602 carries a present-but-null complianceChecks (a .get default does not defend a null), 604 carries a bare string inside the checks list, 605 a null device block, and one row in the data array is a bare string; each costs itself, never the run. namespaced_ids is skipped: the id is the bare numeric Drata id, un-namespaced (reported defect, acknowledged in the README -- one credential can only see one workspace).",
 "kwargs": {
  "url": "$BASE",
  "api_token": "fixture-token"
 },
